<heading>edit - Rename a topic.</heading>

<rule/>

<heading level="2">
Usage
</heading>

<pre>
  edit TOPIC --new-name NAME
</pre>

<heading level="2">
Description
</heading>

<paragraph>
Renames a topic. TOPIC may be an id or a topic name. Topic
names are only unique within their category — if the name is
ambiguous, the matching topics and their categories are shown
and an id must be used. The new name must not collide with
another topic in the same category (case-insensitive).
</paragraph>

<heading level="2">
Examples
</heading>

<pre>
edit "Römisches Reich" --new-name "Römische Kaiserzeit"
  Rename the topic.
</pre>

<heading level="2">
See also
</heading>

<paragraph>
add, delete, list, find
</paragraph>
